<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Office of Supply to seek 2,550T copper.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Office of Supply to seek 2,550T copper.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Office of Supply (OSROK) said it will invite tenders for 2,550 tonnes of copper cathode by 10.30 a.m. (0130 GMT) on November 7.</p>
<p>An OSROK official said the copper must be listed on the London Metal Exchange's deliverable brands of grade A.</p>
<p>The OSROK official said shipment was to be made by December 31 and delivery by January 31 to the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
